{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your care team doctors. You're here today for your scheduled high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been doing this every few months for a while now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Your history shows you're in remission from CNS lymphoma and this is part of your maintenance plan. How have you been feeling overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty well, actually. I had bronchitis a couple weeks ago, but it’s completely gone now. My main issue is these episodes of left facial numbness and trouble speaking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned they happen about once a week, last 30 to 60 minutes, and are triggered by emotion. No loss of consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. It feels like a seizure, but I stay aware. I’m worried it might be the lymphoma coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a valid concern. We’ll monitor that closely. For now, we’ll proceed with your chemotherapy as planned. You’ll get rituximab first, then high-dose methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve restarted my temozolomide too—got the prescription filled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. You’ll continue that at home for 7 days with this cycle. We’ll also give you IV sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys during methotrexate infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin afterward, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2190-04-16 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to help clear the methotrexate. We’ll start it soon after the infusion and monitor your levels daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2190-04-16 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You just finished the methotrexate infusion—8 grams per square meter, as planned. You tolerated it well, no reactions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2190-04-16 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel much during it. That’s a good sign, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2190-04-16 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very good. We’ll start leucovorin now and keep you on sodium bicarbonate to keep your urine alkaline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2190-04-16 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2190-04-16 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for nausea, mouth sores, or low blood counts. But so far, your labs are stable. We’ll check your methotrexate level tomorrow to make sure it’s dropping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level is 0.19—coming down nicely. That means the leucovorin is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But I had another episode last night—left face numb, trouble speaking for about 40 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you told me. We’re concerned it could be seizure activity or possibly related to your lymphoma. We’d like to do a bedside EEG today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "An EEG? Like for seizures?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It checks your brain’s electrical activity. It’s painless and we can do it right here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do it. And what about my lamotrigine? I take 150 mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2190-04-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We sent a blood test to check your level. It’ll help us know if your dose is right for seizure control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The EEG is back—preliminary read is negative. No seizure activity detected during the test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not seizures? Then what’s causing the numbness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could still be partial seizures that didn’t happen during the EEG. Or it might be related to your past lymphoma. We recommend a brain MRI to check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was hoping to avoid another MRI. I have family plans this weekend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. We won’t delay your discharge, but it’s very important you get the MRI early next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do it. I just don’t want to miss my grandson’s birthday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2190-04-17 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely reasonable. We’ll schedule it for Monday with Dr. ___ . You’ll also have a follow-up appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest methotrexate level is 0.13—low enough that you can go home today with oral leucovorin for one more day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your usual medications—desmopressin for diabetes insipidus, lamotrigine, propranolol for anxiety, and the rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lisinopril for blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, restart that today. We held it in the hospital because of the IV fluids and kidney monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. My sodium was low yesterday—127. Is that from the desmopressin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We monitored it closely. It’s improved, and you’re asymptomatic, so we’re not concerned. Just keep drinking water normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the temozolomide—I take it for 7 days starting today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. And finish the leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m a bit nervous about the numbness episodes. Could they be the lymphoma coming back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible, but we don’t know yet. That’s why the MRI is so important. Most recent scans showed no recurrence, so we’re hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if it is back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll adjust your treatment plan. But for now, you’re in good shape—neuro exam is normal, strength is equal in both hands."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2190-04-18 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I’ll keep the MRI appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your discharge instructions include taking leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate for one more day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow up with Dr. ___ for the MRI and lamotrigine level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll get the final EEG report too. Assuming all goes well, your next chemotherapy would be in six months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Six months? That’s a relief. I’d like some time off from hospital visits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best to keep it that way. But please don’t delay the MRI. Call us if you have fever, severe nausea, or another prolonged episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2190-04-19 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2190-04-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in before you leave. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2190-04-19 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Medications, follow-up, MRI—got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2190-04-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll send the discharge summary to your primary team. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2190-04-19 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again. I’ll call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2190-04-19 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your lamotrigine level is still pending. We’ll contact you if we need to adjust the dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2190-04-19 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch for a call."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2190-04-19 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your sodium was low at 127 but stable. Just keep your fluid intake balanced—don’t overdrink."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2190-04-19 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. I know from before how that can go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2190-04-19 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And continue your desmopressin as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2190-04-19 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve confirmed your follow-up MRI is scheduled for Monday morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2190-04-19 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ve already told my son to come with me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2190-04-19 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good idea. We’ll have the results within a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2190-04-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your physical exam today is excellent—alert, strong, no new neurological deficits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2190-04-19 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel strong. Just want to stay ahead of this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2190-04-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing everything right. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2190-04-19 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You can head home now. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2190-04-16 09:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2190-04-19 16:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of CNS B-cell lymphoma in remission was admitted for scheduled high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. He tolerated the infusion well, with methotrexate levels declining appropriately to 0.13 by discharge. He reported ongoing episodes of left facial numbness and dysarthria, concerning for partial seizures or possible disease recurrence. A bedside EEG showed no seizure activity on preliminary review, and a lamotrigine level was sent but remained pending at discharge. The patient declined an in-hospital brain MRI due to prior commitments but agreed to outpatient imaging the following week. His diabetes insipidus and hypertension were managed without complication, and he was discharged home with a plan to complete a short course of leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate, continue his regular medications including temozolomide, and follow up in clinic with MRI and neurology evaluation. The next chemotherapy cycle is anticipated in six months pending outpatient findings.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Unspecified B-cell lymphoma, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Localization-related (focal) (partial) symptomatic epilepsy and epileptic syndromes with simple partial seizures, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Paresthesia of skin",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
